{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
In [Em]eighteen hundred and forty-one
I [D]put my corduroy breeches on,
I [Em]put my corduroy breeches on
To [D]work upon the [Em]railway.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Em]Fil-i-me-oo-ree-i-ree-ay,
[D]Fil-i-me-oo-ree-i-ree-ay,
[Em]Fil-i-me-oo-ree-i-ree-ay,
To [D]work upon the [Em]railway.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
In [Em]eighteen hundred and forty-two
I [D]left the old world for the new,
Bad [Em]cess to the luck that brought me through
To [D]work upon the [Em]railway.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
In [Em]eighteen hundred and forty-three
'Twas [D]then I met sweet Biddy McGee,
An [Em]elegant wife she's been to me
While [D]working on the [Em]railway.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: Em}
